* Diagonal addressing smoke on the NxN MCE weave.
* Pin order matches magnetic_core_64x64.kicad_sch after Sim.Pins.
* Lines are 0-based: X0/Y0, X1/Y1, ... X63/Y63. There is no X64.
* This deck pulses X32/Y32 through X63/Y63.
* X0/Y0 through X31/Y31 start at +Br, the state after those writes.
*
* One CCS each for X, Y, and inhibit, 400 mA. Inhibit stays off.
* Each pulsed core gets one write 1 (1 us rise, 2 us flat, 1 us fall).
* The diagonal and one X half-select neighbor per address are the mce
* devices. Other positions are omitted; each driven line still
* series-connects the cores that sit on it. Sense is the early flat.
*
* Batch: kicad/core_element_sim/models/array64x64_cycle.sh
* Prints RESULT PASS or RESULT FAIL.

.include coremem.cir
.include ccs.cir

.param vdrive=12

Vdrive vdrv 0 DC {vdrive}
Viccsx ccs_x ccs_xin 0
Viccsy ccs_y ccs_yin 0
Viccsi ccs_i ccs_iin 0
Xccs_x ccs_xin ccs ic_half=0.4
Xccs_y ccs_yin ccs ic_half=0.4
Xccs_i ccs_iin ccs ic_half=0.4
Rx ccs_x 0 10Meg
Ry ccs_y 0 10Meg
Ri ccs_i 0 10Meg
Rfold FOLD 0 10k

